Passerelle Baton is a cursive and script typeface tailored specifically for handwriting instruction in primary schools. Designed to meet the pedagogical needs of educators, it facilitates the learning process for young students by focusing on clear, consistent, and easily traceable letterforms.
This project is a modified derivative of the original Marelle font family, which was initially developed by the French Ministry of National Education and originally designed by Laurent Bourcellier, Jonathan Fabreguettes, and Rosalie Wagner. Passerelle Baton introduces several key educational adjustments to the initial design.
Notable updates include the integration of alternative closed "s" glyphs, an increase in uppercase letter proportions to span three interlines instead of two, and refined strokes on specific letters (such as G, K, M, W, and Y) to ensure better weight consistency and easier drawing for early learners.
To contribute, see https://github.com/assoceeeee-cell/Passerelle
